00:48:16.000 --> 00:49:00.000
check every letter in case they found a new ripper letter. This way they would be able to catch it before it was sent so they would be able to determine where exactly it had been posted from. They would end up checking a total of around 15 million letters. Sunderland police and West Yorkshire police were taking different approaches during this phase of the investigation. West Yorkshire completely eliminated suspects from the investigation on the grounds that their voice and handwriting didn't match whereas Sunderland police didn't eliminate them completely from the investigation. They had the view that just because somebody's handwriting didn't match the letters or the voice on the tape didn't mean that person wasn't the

